Subject: venus: no host image copy on macOS

A host image copy (VK_EXT_host_image_copy) is the host driver's to carry out. NVIDIA's (GB10, 580) maps the whole
memory object the image is in for each one, 64 MB in 13 ms, and unmaps it again. The Metal layer reads every frame
WindowServer draws back into its IOSurface that way, twice or more a frame: the renderer's thread spent two thirds of
a CPU in mmap with the GPU 2% busy, and the desktop showed 9 to 23 frames a second. Without the feature the Metal
layer reads back through a buffer: about 50 frames a second, the renderer's thread at 11%. VN_HOST_IMAGE_COPY=1
offers the feature again.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -484,6 +484,15 @@
       feats->extendedDynamicState3RepresentativeFragmentTestEnable = false;
       feats->extendedDynamicState3ShadingRateImageEnable = false;
    }
+
+#if DETECT_OS_APPLE
+   /* A host image copy is the host driver's to carry out, and NVIDIA's maps the whole memory object the image is in
+    * for each one (64 MB, 13 ms) and unmaps it again: the Metal layer reads every frame WindowServer draws back that
+    * way. Without the feature it reads back through a buffer (VN_HOST_IMAGE_COPY=1 offers it again).
+    */
+   if (!debug_get_bool_option("VN_HOST_IMAGE_COPY", false))
+      feats->hostImageCopy = false;
+#endif
 }
 
 static void
